MTEXTBOX v1.0
June 2, 1996
Mike Dickason
Autodesk Mechanical Group

This .ARX file will currently work only with AutoCAD R13c4.  It will 
not work with earlier versions of R13, and is not guaranteed to work
with any version of AutoCAD that might follow R13c4.



DESCRIPTION:

This is a program to implement a version of the AutoLisp (textbox) function
for use with R13 MText.  This program is necessary since the AutoLisp
(textbox) function doesn't handle MText objects.


Once the MTEXTBOX.ARX has been loaded using the ARX or (arx) command, the 
	usage is as follows:


Usage:  (mtextbox <entity name>)

	Where <entity name> is the entity handle of an MText object.  


Returns:
A list of two points.  The points returned by (mtextbox) describe the bounding
box of the MText object as if its insertion point is located at (0,0,0) and its
rotation angle is 0.  The value of the first point specifies the offset from the
text insertion point to the lower-left corner of the smallest rectangle enclosing
the MText.  The second point specifies the upper-right corner of that box.  Regardless
of the orientation of the MText being measured, the point list returned always
describes the bottom-left and upper-right corners of this bounding box.



NOTE:
This implementation of (mtextbox) differs slightly from the AutoLisp (textbox)
function in that mtextbox takes an entity handle as an argument instead of
the entity definition list used by textbox.


